/// The model list, for the model manager's window (P4 task 10): the stored and
/// signed models, the one in use, the next restart's and the last trial, each
/// signed one with its licence. Like `kai:system`, this is a granted interface,
/// not part of `kai:app` (which is frozen): only the app the system image names
/// `models-window` holds the `models` grant, and a component that imports it
/// without the grant does not stage (`Reason::Link`). It reads only. A switch or
/// an import is Kai's `model_use` or `model_fetch`, logged and undoable, so the
/// window asks the person to ask Kai.
///
/// `read` only queues. The host takes the queue after the call, asks the update
/// service for its list, and tells the app the answer in a later call, so a call
/// never waits on the system, and a version rehearsed beside the active one
/// cannot read twice: only the shown version's queue is taken. The answer is the
/// list as `kai-models 1` text, at most one IPC message (8 KiB); the app parses
/// it as it would any input, and a list it cannot parse is one it does not show.
package kai:models@0.1.0;

interface models {
    /// Asks for the list and returns its ticket. Refused (the call traps) when 4
    /// reads are waiting for the host already.
    read: func() -> u32;
}

/// What the update service answered.
interface listing {
    /// The answer to the read with this ticket: the list, or why there is none
    /// (no model store, or the service did not answer; at most 200 printable
    /// ASCII bytes). A ticket is not reused while this instance runs; a new
    /// instance starts again from 0.
    on-listing: func(ticket: u32, outcome: result<string, string>);
}

/// An app that reads the model list: the two halves of the grant.
world models-read {
    import models;
    export listing;
}
